 122:MidiHandler.h ****     /** Call from the main loop every ~50 ms: keeps the UART listen DMA
 123:MidiHandler.h ****      *  alive. B1: after any RX error (framing/noise/overrun, e.g. a DIN
 124:MidiHandler.h ****      *  plug wobble) HAL aborts the RX DMA and libDaisy never restarts it
 125:MidiHandler.h ****      *  (the abort-complete IRQ it waits for is NVIC-disabled), so MIDI-in
 126:MidiHandler.h ****      *  died permanently. CheckError() latches the error; a stop+start
 127:MidiHandler.h ****      *  recovers (HAL_UART_Receive_DMA clears the error code). This must
 128:MidiHandler.h ****      *  not run in the audio ISR: DmaListenStart re-inits HAL with
 129:MidiHandler.h ****      *  tick-based timeouts that freeze inside an ISR. */
 130:MidiHandler.h ****     void ServiceMidiIn()
